# Normalize to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# The conformance suite writes spec/test-vectors/vectors.json on every run.
# Per §18.3, headers, payloads, Seals, verdicts and error codes are byte-stable
# across runs; ES256 signature octets are not, because P-ECDSA uses a random k.
# So a regeneration touches exactly the two ES256 signature lines -- never the
# file's structure. core.autocrlf=true would additionally rewrite the whole file
# to CRLF on checkout, drowning that signal in a diff where every line appears
# changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
